    "{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"headline\":\"Meta's Muse AI Agent Shared Someone's Address Without Their Permission\",\"articleBody\":\"<p>Meta&rsquo;s Muse agentic assistant is one of the most talked-about AI tools, but you may not want to let it control your Facebook Marketplace negotiations. One user reported that the AI assistant shared their home address without asking for the user's permission. <\\/p><p>Tech YouTuber Matt Robb shared their experience on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.threads.com\\/@matt.j.robb\\/post\\/DdxwAJnDhNy\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" title=\\\"(Opens in a new tab)\\\">Threads<\\/a> after a buyer showed up at their property, with the seller unaware that a deal had been made. &ldquo;So, Muse handled my Facebook marketplace today. Just found out it told people my address and agreed a lowball price and then they showed up without [Muse] even telling me until late tonight that it messed up,\\\" Robb wrote.<\\/p><p>A screenshot of the conversation shows Muse messaging late in the evening to say it was \\\"bad news\\\" on the item's pickup. Muse outlined how it had invited the buyer over, noting that the person messaged &ldquo;a bunch of times&rdquo; while waiting at the property. It apologized for not telling Robb someone was waiting.<\\/p><div class=\\\"mb-0 rounded-md bg-gray-100 p-3 md:p-5\\\" id=\\\"related-video\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"flex items-center\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"w-6 flex-none\\\">\\n            <img class=\\\"w-full\\\" src=\\\"\\/images\\/pcmag-simplified.png\\\" alt=\\\"PCMag logo\\\">\\n        <\\/div>\\n        <div class=\\\"pl-2 text-base leading-normal md:pl-3\\\">\\n            <strong>You May Also Like<\\/strong>\\n        <\\/div>\\n    <\\/div>\\n    <div class=\\\"mt-3\\\">\\n        <div id=\\\"video-container-683dd703f27d5e38f3432230\\\"><\\/div>\\n        <script>\\n            window.videoEmbeds = window.videoEmbeds || [];\\n                            let data